---@class workos.AuthorizeSsoControllerRequest
---@field provider_scopes? workos.AuthorizeSsoControllerRequestProviderScopesList Additional scopes to request from the identity provider. Applicable when using OAuth or OpenID Connect connections.
---@field provider_query_params? workos.AuthorizeSsoControllerRequestProviderQueryParamsMap Key/value pairs of query parameters to pass to the OAuth provider. Only applicable when using OAuth connections.
---@field client_id string The unique identifier of the WorkOS environment client.
---@field domain? string Deprecated. Use `connection` or `organization` instead. Used to initiate SSO for a connection by domain. The domain must be associated with a connection in your WorkOS environment.
---@field provider? workos.AuthorizeSsoControllerRequestProvider|string Used to initiate OAuth authentication with various providers.
---@field redirect_uri string Where to redirect the user after they complete the authentication process. You must use one of the redirect URIs configured via the [Redirects](https://dashboard.workos.com/redirects) page on the dashboard.
---@field response_type string The only valid option for the response type parameter is `"code"`. The `"code"` parameter value initiates an [authorization code grant type](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6749#section-4.1). This grant type allows you to exchange an authorization code for an access token during the redirect that takes place after a user has authenticated with an identity provider.
---@field state? string An optional parameter that can be used to encode arbitrary information to help restore application state between redirects. If included, the redirect URI received from WorkOS will contain the exact `state` that was passed.
---@field connection? string Used to initiate SSO for a connection. The value should be a WorkOS connection ID. You can persist the WorkOS connection ID with application user or team identifiers. WorkOS will use the connection indicated by the connection parameter to direct the user to the corresponding IdP for authentication.
---@field organization? string Used to initiate SSO for an organization. The value should be a WorkOS organization ID. You can persist the WorkOS organization ID with application user or team identifiers. WorkOS will use the organization ID to determine the appropriate connection and the IdP to direct the user to for authentication.
---@field domain_hint? string Can be used to pre-fill the domain field when initiating authentication with Microsoft OAuth or with a Google SAML connection type.
---@field login_hint? string Can be used to pre-fill the username/email address field of the IdP sign-in page for the user, if you know their username ahead of time. Currently supported for OAuth, OpenID Connect, Okta, Entra ID, and custom SAML connections.
---@field nonce? string A random string generated by the client that is used to mitigate replay attacks.
---@field prompt? string If set to `login`, forces re-authentication at the identity provider. For supported SAML providers this sets `ForceAuthn="true"` in the SAML request; providers that don't support it are unaffected.

---@alias workos.AuthorizeSsoControllerRequestProvider "AppleOAuth"|"BitbucketOAuth"|"GitHubOAuth"|"GitLabOAuth"|"GoogleOAuth"|"IntuitOAuth"|"LinkedInOAuth"|"MicrosoftOAuth"|"SalesforceOAuth"|"SlackOAuth"|"VercelMarketplaceOAuth"|"VercelOAuth"|"XeroOAuth"

---@alias workos.AuthorizeSsoControllerRequestProviderQueryParamsMap { [string]: string }

---@alias workos.AuthorizeSsoControllerRequestProviderScopesList string[]

---@class workos.AuthorizeUserlandSsoControllerRequest
---@field code_challenge_method? string The only valid PKCE code challenge method is `"S256"`. Required when specifying a `code_challenge`.
---@field code_challenge? string Code challenge derived from the code verifier used for the PKCE flow.
---@field domain_hint? string A domain hint for SSO connection lookup.
---@field connection_id? string The ID of an SSO connection to use for authentication.
---@field provider_query_params? workos.AuthorizeUserlandSsoControllerRequestProviderQueryParamsMap Key/value pairs of query parameters to pass to the OAuth provider.
---@field provider_scopes? workos.AuthorizeUserlandSsoControllerRequestProviderScopesList Additional OAuth scopes to request from the identity provider.
---@field invitation_token? string A token representing a user invitation to redeem during authentication.
---@field max_age? number Maximum allowable elapsed time, in seconds, since the user last actively authenticated. If the last authentication is older than this value, the user is prompted to re-authenticate; a value of `0` forces re-authentication. Only supported when the provider is `authkit`.
---@field screen_hint? workos.AuthorizeUserlandSsoControllerRequestScreenHint|string Used to specify which screen to display when the provider is `authkit`.
---@field login_hint? string A hint to the authorization server about the login identifier the user might use.
---@field provider? workos.AuthorizeUserlandSsoControllerRequestProvider|string The OAuth provider to authenticate with (e.g., GoogleOAuth, MicrosoftOAuth, GitHubOAuth).
---@field prompt? string Controls the authentication flow behavior for the user.
