---@class workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItem
---@field object string Distinguishes the data provider object.
---@field id string The unique identifier of the provider.
---@field name string The display name of the provider (e.g., "GitHub", "Slack").
---@field description string|distilled.Null A description of the provider explaining how it will be used, if configured.
---@field slug string The slug identifier used in API calls (e.g., `github`, `slack`, `notion`).
---@field integration_type string The type of integration (e.g., `github`, `slack`).
---@field credentials_type string The type of credentials used by the provider (e.g., `oauth2`).
---@field scopes workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemScopesList|distilled.Null The OAuth scopes configured for this provider, or `null` if none are configured.
---@field auth_methods? workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemAuthMethodsList The authentication methods supported by this provider (`oauth`, `api_key`, `client_credentials`, or a combination). Defaults to `["oauth"]` if absent.
---@field connection_owner workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemConnectionOwner Who owns connections made through this provider: `user` for connections owned by individual users, or `organization` for a connection shared by every member of the organization. A provider row can exist before any connected account does.
---@field ownership workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemOwnership Use `connection_owner` instead. Legacy spelling of the same value: `userland_user` corresponds to `connection_owner: "user"` and `organization` to `connection_owner: "organization"`.
