---@class workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemConnectedAccount
---@field object string Distinguishes the connected account object.
---@field id string The unique identifier of the connected account.
---@field connection_role workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemConnectedAccountConnectionRole Whether this row is the compatibility connection visible to undeclared clients or a standard peer for plural-aware clients. The role does not indicate preference or creation order.
---@field account_identifier string|distilled.Null A best-effort identifier for the provider account this connection points at. It is correlation metadata, not the connection identifier or a selector.
---@field account_display_name string|distilled.Null A mutable, non-unique display name for the provider account connection.
---@field user_id string|distilled.Null The [User](/reference/authkit/user) identifier associated with this connection.
---@field organization_id string|distilled.Null The [Organization](/reference/organization) identifier associated with this connection, or `null` if not scoped to an organization.
---@field scopes workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemConnectedAccountScopesList The OAuth scopes granted for this connection.
---@field auth_method? workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemConnectedAccountAuthMethod The authentication method used for this connection (`oauth`, `api_key`, or `client_credentials`). Defaults to `oauth` if absent.
---@field api_key_last_4? string|distilled.Null The last four characters of the API key, or `null` for OAuth connections.
---@field client_id? string|distilled.Null The client ID supplied for this connection. Only present when `auth_method` is `client_credentials`.
---@field client_secret_last_4? string|distilled.Null The last four characters of the client secret supplied for this connection, or `null` when it can't be read. Only present when `auth_method` is `client_credentials`.
---@field config? workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemConnectedAccountConfigMap The connection-level configuration values stored for this connection — the fields the provider declares at `installation` scope, excluding secret and undeclared fields. Returned for every authentication method; empty when no stored values can be disclosed.
---@field state workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemConnectedAccountState The state of the connected account: - `connected`: The connection is active and tokens are valid. - `needs_reauthorization`: The user needs to reauthorize the connection, typically because required scopes have changed. `state_reason` explains why when WorkOS invalidated the connection itself. - `disconnected`: The connection has been disconnected.
---@field established_by_user_id? string|distilled.Null The [User](/reference/authkit/user) whose authorization established this connection. `null` when the connection is developer-managed or its establisher is unknown, and when the establishing member lost access to the organization — in which case `state_reason` is `establishing_member_membership_ended`.
---@field state_reason? string|distilled.Null Why WorkOS put the connection in its current `state`, or `null` when there is no WorkOS-recorded reason: - `establishing_member_membership_ended`: The member who established this organization-owned connection is no longer an active member of the organization, so its credentials were cleared. An organization admin must provide new credentials. Additional values may be added; treat an unrecognized value as an unknown reason.
---@field created_at string The timestamp when the connection was created.
---@field updated_at string The timestamp when the connection was last updated.
---@field warnings? workos.DataIntegrationsListResponseDataItemConnectedAccountWarningsList Non-blocking warnings about an explicitly supplied label. Only writes return it, and only when another connection already uses the label; reads omit it.
---@field userlandUserId string|distilled.Null Use `user_id` instead.
---@field organizationId string|distilled.Null Use `organization_id` instead.
